id: pm-csv-lewj
title: Resource admission drops installed extension type/field registries from validation and revision lookup
description: "Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214 (filed 2026-10-29, missed by the blind issue watch). admission.ts on current main still calls resolveItemTypeRegistry(settings) without the active workspace extension registrations in both scan() and the revision-lookup path (locateItem type_to_folder), so an installed extension-defined item type becomes a row_invalid admission rejection and revision reads use a narrower schema than the writer. Verified on main 2026-11-02: the one-argument resolver call remains. The bounded-admission feature that delivered PR #213 is closed, so this regression needs its own fix: activate the target workspace extensions (or pass the resolved registry) before scan and revision lookup, and add an admission regression with an extension-defined type and field."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: admission,extensions,"gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214"
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:16:36.592Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T12:34:27.602Z"
author: pi-glm
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:10:38.120Z",codex-sol,"Reusing this issue owner for gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214 in the G2 adoption PR, linked to pm-csv-sdk-write-fence and companion pm-cli-website-sumw. Activate the explicit target workspace and use its public active type/field registrations in admission, revision reads and compensation; cover real installed schema extensions and cross-workspace isolation."
  "2026-11-06T12:33:57.172Z",codex-sol,"Validation: six real installed-extension tests pass, covering TOON and JSON Markdown source documents, strict unknown-field policy, direct and host-injected admission, cross-workspace isolation, separate-CLI revision conflicts and interrupted representation replay with opaque string/object fields. Disposable admission registry-only revert fails all five admission/isolation tests; omitting registered fields only from representation parsing fails the recovery test. Restored implementation passes 6/6. Existing resource-bound, late-invalid-row, source/settings and revision scenarios remain covered."
